      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "To determine whether attempts to prevent weight gain will increase success rates for stopping smoking."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "DESIGN",
          "content": "16 week, open, randomised study with 1 year follow up."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "SETTING",
          "content": "Obesity unit."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "SUBJECTS",
          "content": "287 female smokers who had quit smoking before but started again because of weight concerns."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "INTERVENTION",
          "content": "Combination of a standard smoking cessation programme with nicotine gum and a behavioural weight control programme including a very low energy diet. A control group was treated with the identical programme but without the diet."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "MAIN OUTCOME MEASURE",
          "content": "Sustained cessation of smoking."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "After 16 weeks, 68/137 (50%) women had stopped smoking in the diet group versus 53/150 (35%) in the control group (P=0.01). Among these women, weight fell by mean 2.1 (95% confidence interval 2.9 to 1.3) kg in the diet group but increased by 1.6 (0.9 to 2.3) kg in the control group (P<0.001). After 1 year the success rates in the diet and control groups were 38/137 (28%) and 24/150 (16%) respectively (P<0.05), but there was no statistical difference in weight gain."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "content": "Combining the smoking cessation programme with an intervention to control weight helped women to stop smoking and control weight."
        }
      ]},
